Inventors_Bench.name = Industrial Workbench
Inventors_Bench.description = Professor Rochester is credited for inventing the first machine that would mark the beginning of the industrial era. In a time where steam machines were everywhere, Rochester's creation was set to dominate the market. Surely factory owners would prefer a compact, energy efficient, and upgradable variant to the machines they currently used. Unfortunately, Rochester forgot one thing: Steam machines were simply way cooler. Despite being better in every way, Industrial machines never truly took off as expected and steam machines continued to dominate the industrial era. The status quo would continue until the modern era when both steam and industrial machines would be left behind for new, modern machines.
